heif_export.h declares the whole API __declspec(dllimport) on Windows unless LIBHEIF_STATIC_BUILD is
defined, so a consumer compiled without it looks for __imp_heif_* and cannot link against the static
libheif built here.  libheif.pc puts the define in Cflags.private, which pkg-config reports only for
`--static --cflags`, and meson before 1.11 never passes --static when asking for compile flags,
whatever prefer_static says.  libvips configured with meson 1.7.0 (Debian trixie's) therefore built
heifload and heifsave against the DLL declarations, and the final mingw link failed on 74 __imp_heif_*
symbols.

Every libheif built here is static, so the define belongs in the public Cflags, where every
pkg-config consumer sees it whatever its build system or version.

--- a/libheif.pc.in
+++ b/libheif.pc.in
@@ -11,5 +11,4 @@
 Requires.private: @REQUIRES_PRIVATE@
 Libs: -L${libdir} -lheif
 Libs.private: @LIBS_PRIVATE@
-Cflags: -I${includedir}
-Cflags.private: -DLIBHEIF_STATIC_BUILD
+Cflags: -I${includedir} -DLIBHEIF_STATIC_BUILD
